From 94fe4d64fee2867a82b1d858e919c5fd78ab3223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hoangvu12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:13:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Docker Sandbox: a chat shows its sandbox while it's made, and
 a Blank picked early stays Blank
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A chat placed on Docker Sandbox from the zeron-dev template (the Laptop,
2026-11-17) sat on "Sending…" under "Unknown device" with no step line,
then failed where no one could see it: Docker can't make a sandbox from
zeron-dev (its own create operation runs out of time, ~4.5 min, and makes
nothing; zgx-dev and zeron-build-l make one in seconds), so the Create
step failed after 240 s.

- Until the sandbox's engine signs in, its device had no row, so every
  device listed the chat under "Unknown device", and the composer, which
  finds a chat's sandbox by its device row, never followed its steps: no
  "Creating sandbox", and no "Creating sandbox failed" with Run again. The
  host device now writes the device a row as the chat is placed: that
  provider's sandbox (`sandbox:<provider>`, never seen online, never a
  host device). The sandbox's engine writes its own over it when it
  starts, and a sandbox's device is forgotten as before when it's gone.
- The template picker opens as the place is picked, while the account's
  templates still load, listing only Blank; a Blank picked then was
  replaced by the first template when the list arrived. Until the list is
  here no template is picked (nil, sent as Blank), and only that is
  defaulted, never a pick.
